    "Generic public inbox helper keeps its transaction, entitlement/student/binding checks and transaction-clock semantics; heartbeat reuses only its already-owned authority core.",
    "Optional savepoint after foreground awaits uses fresh clock for active supervision, legacy five-minute expiry and command expiry; mandatory exact binding/entitlement fence remains immediately before synchronous HTTP.",
    "Native tests cover later message insertion, competing ACK blocked until owned recovery, failed/completed ACK behavior, unavailable-only claim,50-row/newest-first and500-exclusion bounds, school/student/session/device isolation and immutable private hard-off legacy suppression while announcements remain available.",
    "Optional SQL failure is counted, rolls back only optional work and never reports checked=true. Savepoint rollback/release and COMMIT failures propagate. Actual claimed unavailable command rows roll back on final-fence/COMMIT errors; a required-preparation sentinel remains committed while optional claim failure rolls back only its savepoint. Phase acceptance requires zero unexpected optional inbox failures.",
